added I066, I067, I068; dropped I062, I065. Tip is E047 (5.273 s, 0.7550, margin 0.20 pp). I061 (28 px stage) is running; its expected -0.23 pp would use up the whole margin. So the binding need is accuracy gains of ~0.2 pp that can be paired with the cheap time levers left: curriculum, bs 2048, a lower first-stage resolution. Each of those costs ~0.05 pp per 1% of time. Three ideas added: (1) head lr x3 (H1.7.3) as an exploit for margin, since the head axis is the only SGD-group lever that has responded so far. (2) A 16 px first stage (H2.3), extending the E047 trend for a ~2.7% time cut and pairing with any banked gain. (3) An RNG-shift diagnostic run (H4.1.4) that measures the paired re-draw sd on the current base directly; it is discarded whatever the result, to avoid selecting on seeds 0-2. That sd decides whether the +0.15-0.2 pp keeps can be stacked. Dropped I062: its trim is infeasible at the new 0.20 pp margin and it points at a superseded base. Dropped I065: expected slower, and build time is not binding yet. Queue is now 8: I054, I057, I058, I063, I064 plus the three new ideas. One note on D015: it read E046 (Muon lr 0.20) as recovering E041's loss, but E046 sat on the E045 base and was -0.10 pp against it. Keeping Muon lr 0.16 in I057 is therefore right.
